---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Wrapper/Section.astro";
import SectionLabel from "@/components/Site/SectionLabel.astro";
import PixelLink from "@/components/Site/PixelLink.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Toby Balderson, the human behind Electric Sheep."
>
  <Section containerClass="section-split reveal-block" paddingBottom="small">
    <SectionLabel highlight="The human behind the sheep." />
    <p class="statement">
      Toby Balderson founded Electric Sheep in 2023 on a simple idea: technology
      should be built around people, not the other way round. The tools and
      automations he creates free his clients to do more of what they're best
      at.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    paddingTop="none"
    paddingBottom="small"
    containerClass="portrait reveal-block"
  >
    <div class="portrait__frame width-full">
      <img src="/assets/images/toby.jpg" alt="Toby Balderson" />
      <div class="portrait__overlay"></div>
      <span class="portrait__caption">Big nose, bigger ideas.</span>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {
    /* Three literal sections rather than a loop over a local array: the visual
      editor edits copy in place, and an array in the frontmatter would put this
      text out of its reach. */
  }
  <Section
    containerClass="section-split reveal-block"
    paddingTop="small"
    paddingBottom="none"
  >
    <SectionLabel highlight="What he does" />
    <p class="note">
      Strategy, brand, UX and the plumbing behind them. Most studios do the
      pretty part or the technical part. Electric Sheep does both, because a
      brand that doesn't function is just decoration. If a robot can do the
      boring part, Toby will build the robot. The judgement stays human.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    containerClass="section-split reveal-block"
    paddingTop="small"
    paddingBottom="none"
  >
    <SectionLabel highlight="Why sheep?" />
    <p class="note">Do androids dream of electric sheep? Nobody knows. But the question was never really about machines. It was about what makes us human: imagination, curiosity, care.<br /><br /><span>That's why we named the studio after it. We use the best technology available, but the ideas, the taste and the attention to detail are always ours.</span><br /><br /><span>Sheep by name. Not by nature.</span></p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    containerClass="section-split reveal-block"
    paddingTop="small"
    paddingBottom="none"
  >
    <SectionLabel highlight="The studio" />
    <p class="note">10 Minden Street, St Helier, Jersey. The coffee is good &amp; Toby accepts visitors by appointment. </p>
  </Section>

  <Section containerClass="px-hover reveal-block gap-3">
    <PixelLink
      href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/toby-balderson-69b752164/"
      color="var(--text)"
      fontSize={24}>Find Toby on LinkedIn</PixelLink
    >
    <PixelLink href="/contact" color="var(--text)" fontSize={24}
      >Start a conversation</PixelLink
    >
  </Section>
</Layout>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .portrait__frame {
      position: relative;
      height: 32rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-radius: var(--radius-small);
      background-color: var(--surface-placeholder);
    }
    .portrait__frame img {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .portrait__overlay {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background: var(--overlay-protect);
    }
    .portrait__caption {
      position: absolute;
      left: var(--card-pad);
      bottom: var(--space-3);
      font-family: var(--primary-family);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      line-height: var(--line-height-medium);
      color: var(--text-on-image);
    }

    .note {
      font-family: var(--primary-family);
      font-weight: var(--primary-regular);
      font-size: var(--h4);
      line-height: var(--line-height-huge);
      color: var(--text);
      max-width: 60ch;
    }
  }
</style>
